  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Participatory budget monitoring at district and national levels</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a relatively large three-year project, funded by EU and CAFOD, to help East Timorese citizens establish an inclusive and empowered society where district and national governments are accountable to the citizens who elected them for the transparent use of oil and gas reserves.  Luta Hamatuk (LH) works to promote participatory monitoring of government budgets and infrastructure development at district and national-level, and progress on implementing EITI (Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative) standards.  At local level LH works through a network of focal points (community-based volunteers) who are kept updated through periodic briefings, and District Infrastructure Monitoring Committees.  Other activities include robust analysis of the national budget and the Petroleum Fund, research and dissemination of informational, policy and campaigning materials, and networking with civil society organisations at national, regional and international levels.</narrative>
  </description>
